    ('2d000000-0000-4000-8000-020000000101', 'PASSAGE', 'A. Foxes were once rare visitors to British towns, but since the 1980s they have become a familiar sight in suburban gardens. Surveys suggest that a town of a hundred thousand people may now be home to several hundred foxes, most of them living in small family groups.
